  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** RPAY is gaining traction, with organic growth fueled by new enterprise client rollouts and expanded payment channels, especially in Business Payments (normalized for political spending). The transformational acquisition of KUBRA marks a major scale-up in bill payments and customer interaction capabilities, positioning the combined entity for robust reported revenue expansion. Cash flow generation remains positive, though quarterly variability persists.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is actively integrating KUBRA and reiterated an improved margin outlook for 2026, signaling confidence in the combined platform. Strategic emphasis on enterprise implementations and cross-selling is yielding early momentum. The market narrative is bullish, with analysts highlighting substantial upside, while the team navigates non-cash impairment noise and focuses on driving durable free cash flow growth.",
